  "body": "Source: second review of merged PR #2504, https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2504#issuecomment-6979868690\n\n## Items\n\n1. Warning note wording. The warning note reports the total travel below the part bottom (2.803 mm for a 6 mm drill) as \"Break-through\". The user set 1 mm. The note must agree with the field, or name both values.\n\n2. Selector visibility. On a lathe, the axial drill always uses Tip. The page shows \"Full diameter\". The selector also shows where it has no effect: blind holes, a stated Bottom, and tap, ream or spot cycles. Hide or disable the selector in these cases.\n\n3. Decision file. `docs/decisions/2441-drill-point-break-through.md` has two errors:\n   - It says the example projects stay byte-identical. The PR made them new. Correct this statement.\n   - It says MCP patches default to Full diameter. A patch keeps the stored value. Correct this statement.\n\n4. File size. Three files grew past the 400-line limit:\n   - `crates/app/src/stock_sim.rs` (491 lines)\n   - `crates/app/src/stock_play.rs` (410 lines)\n   - `crates/motion/src/drilling/tests.rs` (504 lines)\n   Split each file along a domain seam. The `#[test]` count must not go down.\n\n5. Post coverage. Only the Fanuc and grblHAL posts have a recorded G-code test with a Full-diameter hole. Add one recorded test for each other post. No post code changed, so the risk is low.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Each item above is done, or has its own issue.\n- No `.nc` golden of an existing test changes.\n",
